342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 260 0 R
/T (INTRODUCTION This guidebook offers a comprehensive introduction to entering the corporate world of Sephora under the LVMH group, with a specific focus on the European job market.)
/E (INTRODUCTION This guidebook offers a comprehensive introduction to entering the corporate world of Sephora under the LVMH group, with a specific focus on the European job market.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Initially, our research focused on the LVMH parent group due to its global position in the luxury industry. We then narrowed our focus to Sephora because of its unique role within the group. As both a multi-brand retailer and a brand owner through Sephora Collection, Sephora offers a wider range of career opportunities across functions such as merchandising, marketing, operations, and digital strategy. It must also maintain its own brand identity while working with numerous external brands, which adds complexity to its business model.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (While Sephora is widely recognized in the United States for its position in the beauty retail market, much of the available information is centered on the U.S. context and is relatively easy to access. In contrast, the European market is often difficult to access due to language barriers, its predisposition to informal networking structures, and the generally closed nature of the beauty and luxury industries. However, as the headquarters of both Sephora and LVMH are based in France, Europe represents a key center for decision-making, strategy, and brand development. Furthermore, while Sephora U.S. has well-known competitors such as Ulta Beauty and Sally Beauty, Sephora in Europe occupies a unique position as a leading beauty retailer with a strong brand presence and access to more creative career opportunities due to its proximity to headquarters. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Both Europe and the beauty industry can be challenging fields to break into, especially for those just beginning their job search. This guidebook was designed to address this gap by filtering through the foreign-language materials and combining them with practical insights from interviews with professionals working in Sephora, LVMH-affiliated companies, and related areas within the luxury sector. In doing so, it aims to collect the fragmented information and make it more understandable for students and aspiring job seekers.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
