/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 2354 0 R
/T (Supply Planner Europe The Supply Planner Europe is responsible for purchasing commercial products from suppliers within an assigned budget. They manage order frequencies to optimize logistics costs within a complex remote sourcing environment spanning 3 warehouses and 15 countries. Key duties include securing inventory in warehouses in a timely manner, developing relationships with partner brands, and tracking and communicating KPIs with both internal and external stakeholders. They manage supplier procurement using various Incoterms and coordinate the procurement process for new brand or product launches. They are also responsible for validating logistics, finance, marketing, and quality-related matters, and managing core inventory parameters for the central warehouse. Additionally, they establish purchasing plans for year-end and special events and oversee product lifecycle management and regulatory compliance. Weekly operational tasks include entering supplier orders, tracking transportation, updating order dates, analyzing stock-outs or excess inventory, and implementing corrective actions. They ensure master data is updated based on supplier information, handle quantity and price disputes, and manage supplier returns.)
/E (Supply Planner Europe The Supply Planner Europe is responsible for purchasing commercial products from suppliers within an assigned budget. They manage order frequencies to optimize logistics costs within a complex remote sourcing environment spanning 3 warehouses and 15 countries. Key duties include securing inventory in warehouses in a timely manner, developing relationships with partner brands, and tracking and communicating KPIs with both internal and external stakeholders. They manage supplier procurement using various Incoterms and coordinate the procurement process for new brand or product launches. They are also responsible for validating logistics, finance, marketing, and quality-related matters, and managing core inventory parameters for the central warehouse. Additionally, they establish purchasing plans for year-end and special events and oversee product lifecycle management and regulatory compliance. Weekly operational tasks include entering supplier orders, tracking transportation, updating order dates, analyzing stock-outs or excess inventory, and implementing corrective actions. They ensure master data is updated based on supplier information, handle quantity and price disputes, and manage supplier returns.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
