/T (Q: Why did you choose the luxury fashion industry over the beauty industry? A: I chose the luxury industry because I prefer a slower and more structured work environment. The beauty industry is very fast-paced, highly consumer-facing, and involves a large volume of products \(eg. one lipstick may have 25 varieties of colours\) and frequent launches, which can be overwhelming. In contrast, luxury eyewear has only 3 product launches per year and much longer development cycles \(up to 1.5 years for a single pair of glasses\), which allows me to focus more on the detail, craftsmanship, and technical aspects. I also value the better work-life balance that comes with this type of work.)
/E (Q: Why did you choose the luxury fashion industry over the beauty industry? A: I chose the luxury industry because I prefer a slower and more structured work environment. The beauty industry is very fast-paced, highly consumer-facing, and involves a large volume of products \(eg. one lipstick may have 25 varieties of colours\) and frequent launches, which can be overwhelming. In contrast, luxury eyewear has only 3 product launches per year and much longer development cycles \(up to 1.5 years for a single pair of glasses\), which allows me to focus more on the detail, craftsmanship, and technical aspects. I also value the better work-life balance that comes with this type of work.)
