/T (One of the biggest differences is how time and productivity are managed. In France, there is no strict attendance system. You can typically arrive anytime between 9 and 10 a.m., leave once your work is done, and take breaks freely throughout the day. There is much less direct supervision, which means employees are expected to manage their own time and responsibilities. Performance is evaluated through monthly or annual reviews rather than by how long you stay in the office.)
/E (One of the biggest differences is how time and productivity are managed. In France, there is no strict attendance system. You can typically arrive anytime between 9 and 10 a.m., leave once your work is done, and take breaks freely throughout the day. There is much less direct supervision, which means employees are expected to manage their own time and responsibilities. Performance is evaluated through monthly or annual reviews rather than by how long you stay in the office.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1005 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
