/P 306 0 R
/T (People often have the misconception that employees in France take unlimited breaks, but interestingly, this flexibility actually leads to a faster-paced and more focused work environment. Because people want to finish their work efficiently and leave earlier, they tend to stay very focused during working hours. This is quite different from Korea, where there is often an expectation of staying late, which can sometimes lead to lower efficiency during the day. In contrast, the office environment in Paris is more results-driven, and people tend to work quickly and independently to )
/E (People often have the misconception that employees in France take unlimited breaks, but interestingly, this flexibility actually leads to a faster-paced and more focused work environment. Because people want to finish their work efficiently and leave earlier, they tend to stay very focused during working hours. This is quite different from Korea, where there is often an expectation of staying late, which can sometimes lead to lower efficiency during the day. In contrast, the office environment in Paris is more results-driven, and people tend to work quickly and independently to )
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [4]
>>
