/Title (One key difference I noticed is that in Korea, it is generally more straightforward to apply directly to jobs, whereas in France, the process is much more dependent on networking. I would say it is about 50/50 between applications and referrals, and many of my classmates secured their jobs through connections rather than formal applications. Building genuine relationships became a crucial strategy for me.)
