/Title (Q: What are common misconceptions job seekers have about this role, or "hidden realities" one only learns after joining? A: Like any other job, there is a fantasy regarding the visible results. Especially with global companies, people focus on the "glamorous" side, such as business trips and communicating with foreigners. In reality, there were many days where we worked more than 12 hours. Due to time zone differences, work often extends beyond standard Korean office hours*, and since public holidays differ by country, work tends to occupy most of the day, even while on vacation. *This insight is based on the Korean market and may reflect region-specific working conditions.)
